      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Tags"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Dental and optical cover are optional modules on most international health insurance plans. Whether you have cover depends on which modules you selected when you took out your policy."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Dental Cover"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Basic dental cover typically includes routine check-ups, scale and polish, fillings, and extractions. Comprehensive dental cover may also include crowns, bridges, root canals, and orthodontics. There is usually an annual benefit limit ranging from USD 500 to USD 3,000 depending on your plan."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Optical Cover"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Optical cover typically includes eye tests, prescription glasses or contact lenses up to an annual limit, and in some cases laser eye surgery. Annual optical benefit limits are usually between USD 150 and USD 500."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "How to Check Your Cover"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Check your policy schedule or contact us at hello@asktic.com and we will confirm exactly what dental and optical benefits you have and any applicable limits or waiting periods."
    }
  ],
